{
  "schema_version": "ux-research-markers.v1",
  "version": "2026-09-30.3",
  "verified_at": null,
  "note": "Compiled for Remorsearch UX QA; not transcribed from any other project. Words match case-insensitively; ASCII markers match only at identifier boundaries (a letter or digit may not touch either end), a space inside a marker matches any run of whitespace (none for Korean). Word markers count only on pages with thin main content, and only as notices: outside navigation chrome and links, not quoted, asked about or written as a person's own report (verdict.py). Structural markers (widgets, inputs, script sources, password fields) are checked first. Identity and cafe-level gates (membership, age_identity) feed auth_gate the same way. Promotion, incentive and virtual-person markers are complete disclosure or label forms, never bare words, so a complaint about sponsored posts is not itself flagged; a match is dropped when a negation follows it (guards.negation_after and guards.negation_clause, for example '...받지 않고' or '...작성한 글이 아닙니다'), when it is quoted, or when its sentence is a question. The disclosure wordings follow the KFTC 추천·보증 등에 관한 표시·광고 심사지침 (예규 제499호, issued and effective 2026-06-01), read via the legalize-kr admrule-kr mirror. Text posts disclose in the title or first part since 2024-12-01, so every flag records its position: lead (the title and the first thresholds.promotion_lead_chars characters of the main text), tail (the last thresholds.promotion_tail_chars characters) or body. promotion and promotion_patterns match anywhere; promotion_placed (clear wordings such as '광고입니다') and promotion_labels (foreign labels such as [AD] or #PR, which the KFTC counts as unclear but which still reveal a relationship) match only in the lead or the tail; '#ad' stays an anywhere marker. incentive separates seller-run review events and seller notices from platform-wide review points; every incentive flag is a per-review candidate, never a page-wide cap. virtual_person holds labels and sentences for AI virtual persons (the KFTC rule in force from 2026-06-01). Every flag is a candidate that a verifier confirms before any grade cap applies. anonymous_handles lists default anonymous nicknames that are never an identity ('ㅇㅇ' per the Korean Wikipedia article on 반고정닉; the others unverified); author-key refuses them. Injection patterns are regular expressions; credential and command patterns need a request addressed to the reader. chrome_idents, author_idents and item_idents (each with their own version) feed the reader's structure-based privacy pass (extract.py): elements whose id or class carries a chrome token are page chrome and never reach the agent; tokens that mark a person's label lose every piece of text they hold, in any child element, to an '[author]' placeholder — except text a time element or a keep_in_author_idents token marks and pieces that on their own are only a date, a time, a relative time, a number with an optional unit or a rating; a link inside a label that points at a member or profile URL (the scrubber's profile-URL patterns, privacy.py) drops the same way; repeated per-person items are separated by a '---' line. A platform whose markup needs a token these lists do not carry can add one through the drop and author fields of its routes.json entry.",
  "thresholds": {
    "thin_main_chars": 200,
    "empty_main_chars": 20,
    "shell_visible_chars": 200,
    "suspect_main_chars": 60,
    "standalone_line_chars": 24,
    "promotion_lead_chars": 150,
    "promotion_tail_chars": 200
  },
